{"name":"Rock Bottom","hex":"#484c49","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rock bottom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The very lowest possible level.","The lowest possible state in one’s life, whether mentally, socially, or otherwise; often, a period of extreme mental stress, homelessness, or rejection by all friends and family."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock_bottom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rock Bottom (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Rock Bottom is the second solo album by the English musician Robert Wyatt. It was released on 26 July 1974 by Virgin Records. The album was produced by Pink Floyd's drummer Nick Mason, and was recorded following a 1973 accident which left Wyatt a paraplegic. He enlisted musicians including Ivor Cutler, Hugh Hopper, Richard Sinclair, Laurie Allan, Mike Oldfield and Fred Frith in the recording."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d6/Rwrockbottom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Bottom_(album)","wikidata":"Q263938"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d6/Rwrockbottom.jpg/250px-Rwrockbottom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d6/Rwrockbottom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d6/Rwrockbottom.jpg/250px-Rwrockbottom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARwrockbottom.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/da/Rock_bottom-cover_smaller.jpg/250px-Rock_bottom-cover_smaller.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/Rock_bottom-cover_smaller.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip